// Notes — durable whole-value key/value notes with compare-and-set semantics, per-namespace
// and global capacity caps, idle reclamation, and the three reserved namespaces
// (room-owners/room-allow/room-nonce, plus the ordinary-but-reserved topic namespace) that
// back room ownership for the `rooms` component (see quint-specs/rooms.qnt, which already
// treats owner/allow as an external dependency it only reads the OUTCOME of).
//
// `note_set` is the bare store-level primitive (store.py:1266): it has NO namespace
// awareness at all — by the store's own docstring it provides "no ownership fencing". Every
// namespace rule (room-owners first-claim, room-allow ownership, room-nonce being
// server-only) is enforced ONLY by app.py's `_note_write_gate`, which the three HTTP
// actions call and `note_set` does not. Modeling `note_set` as its own directly-reachable
// action (per the component map) is therefore not a hypothetical: it is exactly how a future
// internal caller that forgets the gate would behave, and `reserved_ns_only_via_gate` below
// is the property that catches it.
//
// Idle reclamation (`_reap`, store.py:751) is folded in as its own environment action
// (`env_note_reaped`) rather than embedded inside every write action: `_reap` is
// throttle-gated (REAP_EVERY) and wall-clock-driven, so — per quint-modeling's
// abstract-time guidance ("a timeout is just the round advancing") — eligibility to reap is
// modeled as an independent nondet event rather than real mtimes. Guard notes
// (room-owners/room-allow/room-nonce) are protected while `roomActivity` is true for their
// room, mirroring `_guards_a_live_room` (store.py:735) — but `roomActivity` is monotonic
// here (never reset), a deliberately MORE PROTECTIVE simplification: a real guard note can
// eventually be reaped once its room itself goes idle, which this model never represents
// (rooms.qnt does not model room idling/deletion either, so this stays consistent with its
// sibling spec).
